WEBVTT

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:04.490
Golgomon took the gang to get their futures told by Shamanmon, the fortune teller.

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:07.830
But just as Shamanmon started the premonition tango, Grumblemon attacked.

00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:09.190
And this time he brought a friend.

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:12.470
With the strength of Gollomon behind him, Grumblemon stole Tommy's spirit.

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:17.010
Then Burning Greymon joined the fight, but he didn't know the difference between good guys and bad guys.

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:20.230
Gogglehead figured out that it was Shamanmon possessed by a beast spirit.

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:23.390
But when he freed Shamanmon, the beast spirit possessed him instead.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:28.070
When he started attacking his friends, Koji had to digivolve to Ken the Goruromon to stop him.

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:29.890
Man, did these guys have control?

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:30.870
What?

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:41.450
Dangerous

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:01.400
Is there anything we can do?

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:03.420
Yes, get out of here before it's too late.

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:07.510
All right, if it's a fight you want, fight me!

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:13.050
Is he really going to try to fight him?

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:14.850
What if they hurt each other?

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.660
Come before one of us gets hurt!

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:33.640
Fire over all!

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:43.800
Something before he levels the whole forest!

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:44.900
Or the whole world!

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:47.020
I'll stop him!

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:58.060
Never have to fight trees! He'll be deadly!

00:02:58.550 --> 00:02:59.970
Then count your blessings we're not true!

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:00.870
Let's go!

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:04.420
I can only spirit evolve to kumamon.

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:17.140
Daydreaming, come on!

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:22.480
And if he keeps this up, they're gonna have to rename it the Burnt to a Crisp Kingdom.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:39.580
Wait, what am I doing?

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:43.620
Leave this how I'm gonna check out.

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:46.950
Gotta stay calm, stay in control.

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:49.720
These guys are my friends.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:51.660
I have to keep reminding myself that.

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:53.290
Wait a second.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:56.920
If they are my friends, why are they attacking me?

00:03:57.580 --> 00:03:58.840
Maybe they are the enemy.

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:18.860
That's why they call it a beast spirit. Isn't it obvious?

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:21.820
But it's like Takuya isn't even in there. Can't we help him?

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:25.120
Not really. He has to learn to control the beast spirit on his own.

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:26.500
Sooner or later, he will.

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:28.460
It's the later part I'm worried about.

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:38.560
I can't believe I said that.

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:40.810
I can't keep running away.

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:42.210
Takuya needs me.

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:44.710
This is going well.

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:49.310
Like before.

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:51.060
Back in the real world.

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:03.240
How did the baby drop his books?

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:05.580
Next thing you know, he's gonna fall down!

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:06.420
We didn't know!

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:11.070
You're a whip, kid!

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:13.780
Another baby!

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:14.710
Oh, no!

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:19.220
Better run, kid!

00:05:19.930 --> 00:05:20.910
What can I do?

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:24.400
Those kids were bigger than me, and Burning Greymon is way bigger!

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:06.850
We're here to kill.

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:35.590
Kami, you have to stop this.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:41.350
It's Kumamon, and you're nothing but a big bully.

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:43.090
No, you're wrong.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.740
Kumamon, you're under the spell of Bakuman's nightmare syndrome.

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:49.180
What you're feeling isn't real. You have to fight it.

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:52.520
You're not my enemy.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:57.630
And the true courage isn't paying bullies back.

00:06:58.150 --> 00:06:59.730
It's just standing up to them.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:04.200
I see that as being a bully.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:06.060
You can't let fear control you.

00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:07.220
You have to fight it.

00:07:12.260 --> 00:07:12.980
We're friends.

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:29.980
Wait, they're going to do...

00:07:31.790 --> 00:07:31.990
Do

00:08:01.530 --> 00:08:02.510
You've destroyed them all!

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:04.450
Some digi-destined I am.

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:12.090
Takuya, are you okay?

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:14.050
I should be asking you that.

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:14.970
Thanks, Tommy.

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:17.620
It was nothing, but you're welcome.

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:18.980
It wasn't nothing.

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:21.320
It was one of the bravest things I've ever seen.

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:23.110
Well, I owed you one.

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:24.170
Now we're even.

00:08:25.050 --> 00:08:26.270
Oh, the trials of friendship.

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:28.970
Take note, you two, for when you get your beast spirits.

00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:29.830
Um.

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:30.920
Why don't you go first?

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:33.250
Oh, no, you. I insist.

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:38.020
Yes, well, of course, you still have to get back those spirits that you lost to Grumblemon.

00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:40.040
Thanks for the reminder.

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:44.580
But what good does it do us if we get all those spirits back and we can't even control them?

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:46.860
How are we going to find Grumblemon anyway?

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:51.300
Geez, it seems harder to avoid him than to find him.

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:54.700
I think we should just keep going. I bet we'll run into him sooner or later.

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:55.880
Sounds good to me.

00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:59.620
I know you want your spirit back, but how can running into Grumblemon sound good?

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.420
That's the dumbest thing I ever heard.

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:03.840
You better hope you'll get your beast spirit first, pal,

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:05.880
because I'm coming after you when I get mine.

00:09:06.140 --> 00:09:08.500
Now I know what Pokemon meant by the trials of friendship.

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:11.940
The book says the roots make the forest paths treacherous.

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:12.860
Oh, that's ridiculous.

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:17.740
Hey, check it out.

00:09:17.960 --> 00:09:18.980
What's up with these roots?

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:22.200
Ooh, do those symbols stand for hugs and kisses?

00:09:22.550 --> 00:09:24.170
Yeah, like you'd know.

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:24.770
Hey!

00:09:25.530 --> 00:09:26.450
It's like a maze.

00:09:26.650 --> 00:09:27.410
Well, not really.

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:28.750
All the roots connect.

00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:29.930
Well, make it a maze.

00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:32.620
Everyone get your own vine, and let's go!

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:33.100
Woo-hoo!

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:34.440
Cool, I'll take this one.

00:09:34.690 --> 00:09:35.970
And this one's mine!

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:37.830
Ready, set, go!

00:09:47.240 --> 00:09:48.940
We win!

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:55.880
Yeah, so what's the big deal?

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:56.380
Whoa!

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:08.030
For you to say, time!

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:21.160
Grumblemon, no!

00:10:21.630 --> 00:10:22.670
Grumblemon, yes!

00:10:23.030 --> 00:10:25.110
And you just where I want you!

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:25.730
Yes!

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.900
Looks like you two won race.

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:34.300
Too bad winners, now big losers.

00:10:34.720 --> 00:10:36.440
It's spirit-taking time.

00:10:36.920 --> 00:10:39.340
Actually, I think it's getting stuck in the mud time.

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:40.420
You not quiet.

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:43.220
You learned hard way at really hammer-smashing time.

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:43.720
Got it?

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:45.820
And now take care of you.

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:47.760
Why can't we just be friends?

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:48.840
Quiet now.

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:51.200
No one give me much trouble as you.

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:52.280
You know you lose.

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:53.900
Why not you play nice?

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:54.640
So what?

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:56.300
We should just hand over our spirits?

00:10:56.660 --> 00:10:57.340
Forget it.

00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:59.930
That's never going to happen, especially now.

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:01.320
I have my beast spirit.

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:04.330
Now I mean not afraid of that.

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:06.700
Well you should be, cause it's very powerful.

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:09.240
Only powerful if you can control.

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:11.780
And I'm betting that you not learn yet,

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:13.400
or why you look so afraid.

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:16.680
See, you tell me all I need know.

00:11:19.140 --> 00:11:19.700
Sorry!

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:23.310
I said you!

00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:31.460
Yeegah smart!

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:09.060
You just had enough fire today?

00:12:09.400 --> 00:12:09.800
Right!

00:12:15.020 --> 00:12:16.060
Fire, please!

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:29.960
If you want it!

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.490
You have him! Take him!

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:35.110
Don't worry. We're fine now.

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:36.590
I mean, we're kind of stuck here.

00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:37.170
Okay.

00:12:38.930 --> 00:12:44.580
Play hide and seek. You really need seek, you know.

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:05.180
Not good either

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:38.180
Are you okay?

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:42.020
Yeah, but Tommy's still in trouble,

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:44.160
and I don't know how to save him.

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:46.460
Looks like a human spirit just can't compete

00:13:46.460 --> 00:13:47.420
with the beast spirit.

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:49.740
You have to turn into Burning Greymon.

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:50.940
But I can't.

00:13:51.210 --> 00:13:52.750
What if I lose control again?

00:13:52.950 --> 00:13:54.780
Don't be afraid.

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:56.720
Just remember what Tommy said.

00:13:57.070 --> 00:13:57.310
Huh?

00:13:59.260 --> 00:13:59.960
The true...

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:03.580
It's just standing up to them.

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:06.150
You helped me see that fighting back in fear

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:07.910
is just as bad as being a bully.

00:14:08.420 --> 00:14:09.920
You can't let fear control you.

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:11.060
You have to fight it.

00:14:11.510 --> 00:14:15.700
I know you won't hurt you remember.

00:14:17.270 --> 00:14:19.680
Wait, me?

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:22.300
Remember who your friends are and you'll be fu-

00:14:23.950 --> 00:14:25.330
Not want to help friends?

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:27.940
Tommy!

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:35.750
Playtime over now give me spirit. You hurry, maybe you save him

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:54.730
Friend you be won't even give a beast spirit to save friend. I'm not afraid of you. You should be

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:07.230
If Tommy can show courage in the face of that freak, then so can I!

00:15:41.450 --> 00:15:42.110
You can control!

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:09.060
Tommy, you okay?

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:09.840
Yeah.

00:16:10.140 --> 00:16:13.410
Hey, check it out! You got control of your beast spirit!

00:16:14.130 --> 00:16:15.210
Thanks to you, buddy.

00:16:15.690 --> 00:16:17.550
I'll help the others now. Go get them!

00:16:17.770 --> 00:16:23.740
Right! You're the one who likes Twist, right?

00:16:24.280 --> 00:16:25.200
Well, enjoy!

00:16:45.490 --> 00:16:47.260
Okay, I'll do it the old routine way.

00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:42.170
And if me tired, you still get defeated, good!

00:17:43.180 --> 00:17:45.960
Did you forget me, warrior?

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:08.050
something too!

00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:09.140
You!

00:18:13.580 --> 00:18:21.950
To catch fire!

00:18:22.610 --> 00:18:22.850
Huh?

00:19:06.300 --> 00:19:07.040
Smith's combined!

00:19:07.720 --> 00:19:09.040
Go to get Zoe's spirit!

00:19:30.990 --> 00:19:33.210
Me make kids pay and pay big time.

00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:35.520
Goody, the beast with brains of dirt

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:37.360
has another incompetent plan, honey.

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:39.260
You couldn't outwit a nitwit.

00:19:39.600 --> 00:19:41.620
What? Who dared that you ran him on?

00:19:41.800 --> 00:19:44.100
How many warriors of water do you know?

00:19:45.940 --> 00:19:47.400
Now listen up, rockhead.

00:19:47.600 --> 00:19:49.180
Stop sneaking around behind our backs

00:19:49.180 --> 00:19:50.620
trying to impress Trubimon.

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:53.880
You back off what I do, no business of you.

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:55.340
Thou art mistaken.

00:19:56.290 --> 00:19:58.350
Mercurymon, warrior of steel.

00:19:58.900 --> 00:19:59.920
Thy thoughtless axe.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.340
reflect badly upon us.

00:20:01.860 --> 00:20:03.420
Thou should study an opponent first,

00:20:03.440 --> 00:20:05.340
not just boorishly rush into battle.

00:20:05.670 --> 00:20:06.610
Got that right.

00:20:07.090 --> 00:20:08.830
Arbormon, warrior of wood!

00:20:09.030 --> 00:20:11.150
Yo, you want I should rough him up for you?

00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:13.370
Enough. Our circle is complete.

00:20:13.550 --> 00:20:15.710
But Deskmon, warrior of darkness...

00:20:15.710 --> 00:20:18.230
Oh, sugar, he wouldn't join us in a million years.

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:20.800
Forsooth, he hath no heart for battle,

00:20:20.860 --> 00:20:22.760
and does little more than stare at the moons.

00:20:23.060 --> 00:20:24.680
We shall rule this world,

00:20:24.880 --> 00:20:26.840
whilst his only domain shall be the world

00:20:26.840 --> 00:20:28.800
he sees when he closeth his eyes.

00:20:32.120 --> 00:20:33.940
I'm surrounded by buffoons.

00:20:36.340 --> 00:20:37.460
Isn't that pretty?

00:20:37.950 --> 00:20:39.260
Yeah, I guess.

00:20:40.770 --> 00:20:43.230
Come on, guys. We've got a long road ahead of us.

00:20:45.210 --> 00:20:49.130
That's for sure. They barely beat Gigasmon, and now there are four other bad guys?

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:53.070
This could get ugly on the next Digimon Digital Monsters!
